  "content": {
    "id": "v2-1e331-p64-practice-slot-12-upper-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find values of $k$ for which the parabola $y=x^{2}+2kx+k+6$ is always above the $x$-axis.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-2<k<3$",
      "worked": "The parabola opens upwards, so it is always above the $x$-axis when $\\Delta<0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(2k)^{2}-4(1)(k+6)\\\\&=4k^{2}-4k-24\\\\4k^{2}-4k-24&<0\\\\k^{2}-k-6&<0\\\\(k-3)(k+2)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe parabola $y=k^{2}-k-6$ opens upwards with intercepts $-2$ and $3$. It is below the axis between these intercepts.\n$$-2<k<3$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
